{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mira_vellan","name":"Mira Vellan","role":"protagonist","description":"A seventeen-year-old apprentice cartographer at Silverspine Academy, Mira is lanky and ink-stained, with wind-tangled copper hair and a satchel of brass calipers. Raised by a bridge-surveyor mother who vanished on a failing span, she has charted the skybridge network since childhood and keeps her mother's worn compass.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To discover why her mother's skybridge failed and prevent another family from suffering the same loss.","goal":"Chart and repair the failing skybridges before the isles drift apart.","flaw":"Reckless self-reliance; she hides her doubts and refuses help until it is too late.","internal_conflict":"She fears the maps she trusts are wrong, which would mean her mother's death was preventable by her own knowledge.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls and Warden red tape block her access to the critical spans she must survey and mend.","arc":"Mira begins as a solitary, secretive apprentice who works alone to avoid being proven wrong. When a span she surveyed alone frays during a Toll War blockade and she needs Emberroost braiders to save it, she is forced to share her flawed charts openly. She ends as a leader who coordinates Wardens, millers and merchants to rebuild the network, accepting that collaboration is stronger than certainty.","personality_traits":["curious","stubborn","observant","secretive","brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Surveying","description":"Reads cloudstone tension and drift patterns to predict where a span will fail.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Wind Sense","description":"Feels shifts in air currents through years of crossing bridges.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_torren_ashgrave","name":"Torren Ashgrave","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered master braider at Emberroost with soot-darkened forearms and a gray beard singed at the tips. Once Mira's mother's partner on the bridge crews, he carries a limp from the collapse that took her.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To atone for surviving the collapse that killed Mira's mother by ensuring the craft he teaches never fails again.","goal":"Forge a new generation of cloudstone cable strong enough to withstand the drift.","flaw":"Guilt-driven secrecy; he withholds what he knows about the collapse.","internal_conflict":"He wants to confess a mistake in the braiding but fears losing his place as the Wardens' respected master.","external_conflict":"Wardens leadership rations cloudstone and forbids experimental braiding while the Toll War drains resources.","arc":"Torren starts as a guarded mentor who deflects questions about the old collapse. When Mira finds his flawed braid pattern in the failing span, he must choose between his reputation and the truth. He confesses publicly and teaches the corrected weave, ending as an honest teacher at peace with his past.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","guilt-ridden","skilled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Weaves cloudstone cables of exceptional strength inside shielded forge-pits.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_sabine_korrigan","name":"Sabine Korrigan","role":"antagonist","description":"A poised Drift Cartel merchant princess in her forties at Mistral Docks, always dressed in layered storm-silk and rings stamped with shipping-lane seals. She rose from a dockhand's family by mastering the Cartel Charter.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure lasting safety and wealth for her family after growing up in dock poverty.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and control which isles are reconnected.","flaw":"Control obsession; she treats every person and bridge as an asset to be leveraged.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her tolls are accelerating the bridges' decay but cannot abandon the profit that shields her family.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and Hollow Circle resist her tolls and grain levy, threatening Cartel dominance.","arc":"Sabine begins as a calculating profiteer who blocks Mira's surveys to protect toll revenue. When a Cartel ship is stranded by a severed span and wind-debt ruins her own crew, she faces the cost of her policy. She suspends the tolls and funds repairs, ending as a wary ally who learns safety cannot be owned.","personality_traits":["shrewd","charming","ruthless","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Negotiation","description":"Bargains shipping rights and wind-debt terms with ruthless skill.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_thistledown","name":"Oren Thistledown","role":"supporting","description":"A cheerful young miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted hair and sun-browned hands, Oren grew up during the long memory of the Great Calm tales and runs his family's windmill.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep his village fed and free from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Deliver grain across failing bridges and win relief from the levy.","flaw":"Naive optimism; he trusts anyone who smiles and ignores warning signs.","internal_conflict":"He longs to see the wider isles but feels bound by duty to the mill.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy and failing bridges threaten his harvest deliveries.","arc":"Oren starts as an easygoing miller who believes Sabine's agents will deal fairly. When a levy collector seizes his shipment and strands him on a failing span, he learns the cost of naive trust. He becomes Mira's guide and a shrewd negotiator for the Hollow Circle, finally leaving his mill's shadow to travel the isles.","personality_traits":["cheerful","generous","trusting","hardworking"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Reads wind patterns and weather from the turning of mill sails.","category":"other"},{"name":"Easy Rapport","description":"Quickly befriends strangers and gains their cooperation.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mira_torren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_torren_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Torren Ashgrave mentors Mira Vellan in braiding, while secretly concealing his role in the collapse that killed her mother, which strains their bond."},{"id":"rel_sabine_mira_rival","source_character_id":"chr_sabine_korrigan","target_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sabine Korrigan obstructs Mira Vellan's surveys to protect Cartel toll revenue, putting them at odds over who controls the skybridges."},{"id":"rel_sabine_oren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_sabine_korrigan","target_character_id":"chr_oren_thistledown","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Sabine Korrigan's grain levy squeezes Oren Thistledown's family mill, making her his main antagonist."},{"id":"rel_oren_mira_ally","source_character_id":"chr_oren_thistledown","target_character_id":"chr_mira_vellan","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Oren Thistledown guides Mira Vellan across the isles and supplies her crews with grain, amplifying her fight against the Cartel's tolls."}]}
