[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, weathered skybridge courier in her early thirties, born on Mistral Docks to a family of wind-debt defaulters. She wears a patched leather coat lined with cloudstone thread, carries a sealed satchel across the bridges, and has a scar along her left palm from a cable burn. She has crossed more skybridges than anyone alive and knows the drift's rhythms by feel.","personality_traits":["observant","stubborn","dry-humoured","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bridge Sense","description":"Reads tension and sway in skybridge cables to anticipate collapses and wind shifts.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Route Memory","description":"Recalls the shifting skybridge network and its crossing costs in precise detail.","category":"mental"}],"motivation":"To clear her family's inherited wind-debt and earn a settled place she does not have to keep crossing toward.","goal":"Deliver a strange sealed message, found woven into a cloudstone cable, to the one authority able to decode it before the Cartel seizes it.","flaw":"She trusts only what she can carry herself, so she refuses help and withholds information from allies.","internal_conflict":"She longs to belong somewhere but fears that stopping would turn her into the debtor her family was.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants the message and holds her debt over her, while the Toll War closes the bridges she needs.","arc":"Starts as a lone courier who hides the message and distrusts everyone. Pivotal moment: when the Cartel's tolls cut the bridge to Silverspine, she must entrust the message to Corvin Ashe and the Wardens to get it across. She ends as a courier who shares the burden and chooses a home at Silverspine.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":null},{"id":"chr_corvin_ashe","name":"Corvin Ashe","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered, soot-stained Bridge Warden engineer in his fifties from Emberroost, with singed grey eyebrows and burn-pocked forearms. He has braided cloudstone cable for thirty years and keeps a ledger of every bridge he has mended. He is quietly devoted to the network the First Weaving created.","personality_traits":["patient","gruff","meticulous","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and splices cloudstone cable stronger than standard work.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Structural Insight","description":"Diagnoses weaknesses in bridge anchors by sound and vibration.","category":"technological"}],"motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe so no more crossers fall, as happened to his brother.","goal":"Keep the Silverspine bridge open and learn what the strange cable message says about how the first bridges were made.","flaw":"He is rigidly bound to Warden protocol and refuses any shortcut, even a justified one.","internal_conflict":"He reveres the old bridge-makers but fears their message may prove the Wardens' methods wrong.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls choke his funding and the Toll War pits the Wardens against merchants who want bridges open at any risk.","arc":"Starts as a protocol-bound engineer who dismisses unorthodox ideas. Pivotal moment: Isolde's cable shows a braiding pattern the Wardens have never used, and during the Toll War he must break protocol to rebuild a bridge using it. He ends as a flexible mentor who adapts tradition.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_marek_dross","name":"Marek Dross","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished Drift Cartel merchant prince in his forties from Mistral Docks, dressed in sail-silk and rings stamped with Cartel seals. He is courteous and calculating, and he manages debts as other men manage gardens. He believes that controlling trade keeps the archipelago from chaos.","personality_traits":["charming","ruthless","patient","calculating"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt records to coerce people into service.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade Network","description":"Commands informants and shippers across every isle's lanes.","category":"social"}],"motivation":"To secure permanent Cartel control of the skybridges so the archipelago never again faces the stranding of the Great Calm.","goal":"Seize the builders' message and use it to claim legal authority over every skybridge.","flaw":"He believes everyone can be bought or bound, so he underestimates loyalty.","internal_conflict":"He claims to protect the isles but knows his tolls are starving the Hollow Circle.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist the Cartel levy and tolls, and Isolde holds the message he wants.","arc":"Starts as a confident broker who sees people as debts. Pivotal moment: the Grain Levy backlash from the Hollow Circle exposes Cartel greed and costs him his allies. He ends exposed, forced to negotiate and to concede that his control cannot last.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_wren_tallow","name":"Wren Tallow","role":"supporting","description":"A young Hollow Circle miller of nineteen from The Hollow, with flour-dusted hair, calloused hands and a wide, nervous smile. She sends grain across the archipelago and has never left her isle until the levy forces her onto the bridges.","personality_traits":["earnest","curious","anxious","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Predicts wind shifts from windmill behaviour and weather signs.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Grain Accounting","description":"Tracks harvests, shipments and levies precisely to expose false tallies.","category":"mental"}],"motivation":"To keep her family's mill running and stop the Cartel starving the Hollow.","goal":"Carry proof of the Cartel's inflated Grain Levy to Silverspine so the scholars will publish it.","flaw":"She is naive and overshares with strangers.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay safe in the Hollow yet feels shame at letting others fight for her.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens her mill and Marek's agents are watching grain shipments.","arc":"Starts as a sheltered miller who talks freely to strangers. Pivotal moment: she accidentally reveals Isolde's route to a Cartel agent on the bridge, nearly costing the message, and has to face the consequences. She ends as a guarded, confident advocate who testifies against the levy.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_sabine_orrel","name":"Sabine Orrel","role":"supporting","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy in her seventies, thin and sharp-eyed, with ink-stained fingers and a magnifying lens on a chain. She has charted the skybridge network for fifty years and obsesses over its hidden patterns.","personality_traits":["brilliant","secretive","exacting","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pattern Decoding","description":"Finds structure in bridge layouts and cable weaves.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cartography","description":"Maps shifting bridge routes and drift predictions.","category":"technological"}],"motivation":"To complete her life's work: a map that explains why the bridges were woven as they were.","goal":"Decode the builders' message and use it to finish her map of the original network.","flaw":"She hoards knowledge and delays sharing findings until they are perfect.","internal_conflict":"She wants recognition for her life's work but fears that the message will prove her theories wrong.","external_conflict":"Marek Dross pressures the Academy for access to its charts and the Toll War limits her access to materials.","arc":"Starts as a secretive scholar who withholds partial findings. Pivotal moment: Marek's agents threaten the Academy's archives, and she must publish an incomplete decoding to protect it. She ends as a scholar who values open knowledge over perfection.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_marek_debt","source_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marek Dross holds Isolde Vane's family wind-debt and uses it to coerce her into surrendering the builders' message, which turns every delivery she makes into a threat."},{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_trust","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vane reluctantly turns to Corvin Ashe for help crossing the broken bridge, and her distrust of sharing the message strains their alliance."},{"id":"rel_corvin_marek_toll","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Ashe opposes Marek Dross over the Cartel's rising bridge tolls, which starve the Wardens of repair funds."},{"id":"rel_wren_marek_levy","source_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","target_character_id":"chr_wren_tallow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marek Dross's Grain Levy threatens Wren Tallow's family mill, and his agents track her as she carries evidence of the levy's inflated tallies."},{"id":"rel_wren_isolde_guide","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_wren_tallow","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Isolde Vane guides Wren Tallow across the skybridges to Silverspine, though Wren's loose talk puts Isolde's route at risk."},{"id":"rel_sabine_isolde_message","source_character_id":"chr_sabine_orrel","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sabine Orrel wants Isolde Vane's message to decode, but her secrecy and Isolde's guarded nature create friction over who controls it."},{"id":"rel_sabine_corvin_craft","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_sabine_orrel","relationship