:"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt records to coerce people into service.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade Network","description":"Commands informants and shippers across every isle's lanes.","category":"social"}],"motivation":"To secure permanent Cartel control of the skybridges so the archipelago never again faces the stranding of the Great Calm.","goal":"Seize the builders' message and use it to claim legal authority over every skybridge.","flaw":"He believes everyone can be bought or bound, so he underestimates loyalty.","internal_conflict":"He claims to protect the isles but knows his tolls are starving the Hollow Circle.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist the Cartel levy and tolls, and Isolde holds the message he wants.","arc":"Starts as a confident broker who sees people as debts. Pivotal moment: the Grain Levy backlash from the Hollow Circle exposes Cartel greed and costs him his allies. He ends exposed, forced to negotiate and to concede that his control cannot last.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_wren_tallow","name":"Wren Tallow","role":"supporting","description":"A young Hollow Circle miller of nineteen from The Hollow, with flour-dusted hair, calloused hands and a wide, nervous smile. She sends grain across the archipelago and has never left her isle until the levy forces her onto the bridges.","personality_traits":["earnest","curious","anxious","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Predicts wind shifts from windmill behaviour and weather signs.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Grain Accounting","description":"Tracks harvests, shipments and levies precisely to expose false tallies.","category":"mental"}],"motivation":"To keep her family's mill running and stop the Cartel starving the Hollow.","goal":"Carry proof of the Cartel's inflated Grain Levy to Silverspine so the scholars will publish it.","flaw":"She is naive and overshares with strangers.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay safe in the Hollow yet feels shame at letting others fight for her.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens her mill and Marek's agents are watching grain shipments.","arc":"Starts as a sheltered miller who talks freely to strangers. Pivotal moment: she accidentally reveals Isolde's route to a Cartel agent on the bridge, nearly costing the message, and has to face the consequences. She ends as a guarded, confident advocate who testifies against the levy.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_sabine_orrel","name":"Sabine Orrel","role":"supporting","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy in her seventies, thin and sharp-eyed, with ink-stained fingers and a magnifying lens on a chain. She has charted the skybridge network for fifty years and obsesses over its hidden patterns.","personality_traits":["brilliant","secretive","exacting","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pattern Decoding","description":"Finds structure in bridge layouts and cable weaves.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cartography","description":"Maps shifting bridge routes and drift predictions.","category":"technological"}],"motivation":"To complete her life's work: a map that explains why the bridges were woven as they were.","goal":"Decode the builders' message and use it to finish her map of the original network.","flaw":"She hoards knowledge and delays sharing findings until they are perfect.","internal_conflict":"She wants recognition for her life's work but fears that the message will prove her theories wrong.","external_conflict":"Marek Dross pressures the Academy for access to its charts and the Toll War limits her access to materials.","arc":"Starts as a secretive scholar who withholds partial findings. Pivotal moment: Marek's agents threaten the Academy's archives, and she must publish an incomplete decoding to protect it. She ends as a scholar who values open knowledge over perfection.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_marek_debt","source_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marek Dross holds Isolde Vane's family wind-debt and uses it to coerce her into surrendering the builders' message, which turns every delivery she makes into a threat."},{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_trust","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vane reluctantly turns to Corvin Ashe for help crossing the broken bridge, and her distrust of sharing the message strains their alliance."},{"id":"rel_corvin_marek_toll","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvin Ashe opposes Marek Dross over the Cartel's rising bridge tolls, which starve the Wardens of repair funds."},{"id":"rel_wren_marek_levy","source_character_id":"chr_marek_dross","target_character_id":"chr_wren_tallow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marek Dross's Grain Levy threatens Wren Tallow's family mill, and his agents track her as she carries evidence of the levy's inflated tallies."},{"id":"rel_wren_isolde_guide","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_wren_tallow","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Isolde Vane guides Wren Tallow across the skybridges to Silverspine, though Wren's loose talk puts Isolde's route at risk."},{"id":"rel_sabine_isolde_message","source_character_id":"chr_sabine_orrel","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sabine Orrel wants Isolde Vane's message to decode, but her secrecy and Isolde's guarded nature create friction over who controls it."},{"id":"rel_sabine_corvin_craft","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashe","target_character_id":"chr_sabine_orrel","relationship