{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered private investigator in her forties who operates out of a cramped office above the cargo sheds of Mistral Docks. A former Bridge Warden surveyor, she left the service after a disputed bridge-toll audit and now takes cases the Wardens will not touch. She wears a salt-stained oilskin coat, carries a notebook of cross-checked alibis, and has a faint scar across her left palm from a cable burn.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":null,"motivation":"To prove that truth can still be pinned down in a city where everyone lies, redeeming her broken career.","goal":"Unmask the blackmailer and recover the letters before they ruin the people named in them.","flaw":"She trusts only evidence she has verified herself, and so dismisses honest help.","internal_conflict":"She fears her own audit-era judgment was wrong and that she once ruined an innocent man.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel obstructs her inquiries at the docks while the blackmailer keeps one step ahead of her.","arc":"Starts as a lone investigator who refuses to rely on anyone's word. When Tobin Hale's alibi is confirmed only by a witness she had dismissed, she is forced to accept testimony she cannot verify herself. She ends willing to share evidence and trust allies, closing the wound of her old audit.","personality_traits":["dry-witted","stubborn","observant","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Alibi Cross-Checking","description":"Reconstructs timelines from wind-debt ledgers, crossing records and dock logs to expose false alibis.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bridge Surveyor's Eye","description":"Reads cable wear and skybridge crossing patterns to tell who traveled where.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_hale","name":"Tobin Hale","role":"supporting","description":"A lean, soft-spoken Cartel shipping clerk at Mistral Docks, in his thirties, with ink-stained cuffs and a nervous habit of straightening his collar. He keeps the manifests that record every crossing and cargo in and out of the port.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To escape a mountain of wind-debt that is bleeding his family.","goal":"Keep his job and pay off his wind-debt without anyone learning he falsified manifests.","flaw":"Cowardice: he lies reflexively when frightened.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be honest but is ashamed of the small frauds that kept his family afloat.","external_conflict":"Cartel auditors are closing in on his altered manifests, and Mara's inquiry threatens to expose him.","arc":"Starts as a clerk who lies to protect himself and becomes Mara's prime suspect. When Mara confronts him with the manifest discrepancies, he chooses to confess the falsified entries and give her the true dock logs. He ends having traded his safety for honesty and clears his own name.","personality_traits":["anxious","meticulous","evasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Manifest Forgery","description":"Alters cargo records so the changes pass casual inspection.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_kerr","name":"Isolde Kerr","role":"antagonist","description":"A poised cartographer at Silverspine Academy in her fifties, silver-haired and always in immaculate grey. She charts skybridge routes and so knows who crossed where and when, and she has quietly used that knowledge to gather secrets.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To fund the Academy's failing archive and secure her legacy against the Cartel's rising tolls.","goal":"Collect enough payments to buy the Academy's independence from Cartel and Warden control.","flaw":"Righteous pride: she believes the ends excuse any method.","internal_conflict":"She sees herself as a guardian of knowledge yet is becoming exactly the kind of exploiter she despises.","external_conflict":"Mara's investigation and the Toll War strain the Wardens, who may expose her if the blackmail trail leads to the Academy.","arc":"Starts as a self-justified blackmailer who believes she is saving the Academy. After Mara traces her route charts to the extorted letters, she tries to frame Tobin Hale to protect her scheme. She ends exposed and stripped of her post, her pride undone by the very maps she drew.","personality_traits":["composed","calculating","proud","charming"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route Cartography","description":"Reconstructs any traveler's skybridge crossings from charts and records.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Polite Menace","description":"Delivers threats in courteous language that leaves no evidence.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_oakley","name":"Bram Oakley","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Hollow miller in his sixties with flour-dusted forearms and a booming laugh gone quiet of late. His windmill grinds grain for the Cartel's levy shipments, and he is one of the blackmail victims.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his granddaughter's future and the Hollow Circle's name from scandal.","goal":"Get his compromising letter back without his neighbors discovering he once sold grain secretly to the Cartel.","flaw":"Shame-driven secrecy keeps him from asking for help.","internal_conflict":"He loyally upholds the Circle's honesty yet broke it to survive the Grain Levy.","external_conflict":"The blackmailer demands payment while the Cartel's grain levy leaves him with little to pay.","arc":"Starts by paying the blackmailer in secret and refusing to speak. When the blackmailer raises the demand beyond his means, he swallows his shame and gives Mara his letter and story. He ends by confessing to the Hollow Circle and regaining his standing.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Milling Craft","description":"Knows the grain trade and who ships what across the isles.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobin_suspect","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Voss suspects Tobin Hale because his alibi rests on manifests he altered, and her pressure pushes him toward confession."},{"id":"rel_isolde_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_kerr","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Kerr, the hidden blackmailer, sees Mara Voss as the one threat to her scheme and works to mislead and discredit her."},{"id":"rel_isolde_tobin_frame","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_kerr","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Kerr plants evidence to frame Tobin Hale as the blackmailer, exploiting his known falsifications."},{"id":"rel_bram_mara_client","source_character_id":"chr_bram_oakley","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bram Oakley becomes Mara Voss's informant, giving her the letter that links the blackmail demands to Silverspine."},{"id":"rel_isolde_bram_victim","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_kerr","target_character_id":"chr_bram_oakley","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Kerr extorts Bram Oakley by threatening to reveal his secret grain sales to the Cartel."}]}
</Output>
