{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","description":"A forty-one-year-old salvage captain from Mistral Docks, weathered and wiry, with salt-grey braids and a burn scar across her left palm from a forge accident. She built her crew from debtors and drifters, and she carries a ledger of every wind-debt she still owes. She wears a patched oilskin coat and keeps a brass compass that no longer points true.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To clear the crushing wind-debt she owes the Drift Cartel so her crew is no longer indentured to it.","goal":"Recover the liner's strongbox and bring every crew member back alive.","flaw":"She treats people as line items on a ledger and cannot ask for help.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her crew but keeps trading their safety for the payout that would free them.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's debt collector expects the salvage within a season, while the fog-bound liner is picking off her crew.","arc":"Mara begins by gambling her crew's lives to settle the Cartel debt. When Tobin vanishes into the fog-choked corridors, she abandons the strongbox hunt to search for him and trusts Ilsabet's knowledge of the ship. She ends by cutting the liner loose, accepting the debt and a crew that now trusts her.","personality_traits":["pragmatic","guarded","stubborn","fiercely loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Navigation","description":"Reads wind currents and fog banks to steer a vessel through dangerous air.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Hard Bargaining","description":"Negotiates tolls and debts with Cartel agents.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_ash","name":"Tobin Ash","description":"A nineteen-year-old rigger from Emberroost with soot-darkened fingers and a nervous laugh. He braided cloudstone cable as an apprentice before fleeing the forge-island after a failed apprenticeship. He is lanky, wears oversized gloves, and hums to calm himself.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove he is more than a washed-out apprentice and earn a place among the Wardens.","goal":"Secure the liner's rigging and winches so the crew can tow it out of the fog.","flaw":"He cannot resist exploring dangerous places alone to impress others.","internal_conflict":"He craves approval but is terrified that his reckless courage hides a coward.","external_conflict":"The liner's lower decks lure him with voices that mimic the Wardens who rejected him.","arc":"Tobin starts as an eager show-off who wanders off alone. Lured by voices imitating his old Warden master, he is trapped in the flooded lower hold. Mara's rescue teaches him that real skill means working with the crew, and he ends as a steady rigger who calls for help when he needs it.","personality_traits":["eager","impulsive","anxious","inventive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Splices and repairs cloudstone rigging quickly.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsabet_crane","name":"Ilsabet Crane","description":"A sixty-year-old cartographer from Silverspine Academy, thin and silver-haired, with ink-stained cuffs and a rasping voice. She once charted the lane where the liner disappeared and has hidden her faulty survey for decades. She carries rolled charts in a leather tube.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To atone for the mistaken chart that sent the liner into the drift.","goal":"Find the ship's bridge log to learn what truly happened to its passengers.","flaw":"She hoards knowledge and lies by omission to protect her reputation.","internal_conflict":"She needs the truth about the liner but fears it will prove her chart caused the tragedy.","external_conflict":"The ghostly passengers know her name and press her to confess before they release anyone.","arc":"Ilsabet starts out concealing her connection to the liner. In the captain's cabin she finds her own survey tucked in the log, and when the spectral passengers confront her she confesses to Mara. Sharing the safe route she remembers frees her from guilt and lets the crew escape.","personality_traits":["precise","secretive","haunted","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Chart Memory","description":"Recalls the layout of skybridge routes and ship plans in detail.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_captain_edrin_hale","name":"Captain Edrin Hale","description":"The spectral master of the luxury liner, appearing as a tall man in a salt-rimed uniform with hollow eyes. Decades ago he refused to abandon his passengers when the ship drifted off the charted lane. He now binds the vessel and everyone aboard to its fog.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep his passengers from ever being lost again by holding them aboard forever.","goal":"Collect the salvage crew as a replacement complement before the ship drifts on.","flaw":"He cannot accept that guarding people is different from imprisoning them.","internal_conflict":"He remembers the duty to deliver passengers safely but has twisted it into keeping them captive.","external_conflict":"Mara's crew threatens to cut the ship loose and break the fog that sustains him.","arc":"Hale begins as a ruthless keeper who traps intruders. When Ilsabet confesses her chart error and Mara offers to tow the liner to port, he sees that his duty was always to deliver them. He releases the fog and lets the ship be moored, finally ending his watch.","personality_traits":["dutiful","cold","grief-stricken","commanding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fog Command","description":"Summons and thickens fog to disorient and separate intruders.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Voice of the Lost","description":"Mimics the voices of people the listener fears to disappoint.","category":"supernatural"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobin_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobin_ash","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Voss mentors Tobin Ash as his captain, but her habit of valuing him by his output pushes him to take reckless risks that endanger the crew."},{"id":"rel_ilsabet_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilsabet_crane","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilsabet Crane is Mara Voss's reluctant ally, giving her ship knowledge while hiding her past, a secret that threatens their trust."},{"id":"rel_hale_ilsabet_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_captain_edrin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_ilsabet_crane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Captain Edrin Hale blames Ilsabet Crane's faulty chart for his ship's doom and uses the ghostly passengers to pressure her into confessing."},{"id":"rel_hale_mara_rival","source_character_id":"chr_captain_edrin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Captain Edrin Hale and Mara Voss are rival captains, each unwilling to surrender command of the liner and the lives aboard it."}]}
</Output>
