[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered skybridge pathfinder in her late thirties, raised on Mistral Docks among cargo haulers. She wears a patched storm-coat, carries a coil of cloudstone cable on her shoulder, and has a scar across her left palm from a snapped bridge line. Once the best guide in the archipelago, she quit after her last expedition vanished into the overgrown jungle that has swallowed an old isle.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"She wants to clear a crushing wind-debt owed to the Drift Cartel so she can stop crossing bridges for hire.","goal":"Lead the expedition into the jungle ruins and return alive with enough payment to settle her debt.","flaw":"She distrusts everyone and refuses help, hiding fear behind sarcasm.","internal_conflict":"She feels guilty for surviving the last expedition and believes she is cursed to lose anyone she leads.","external_conflict":"The Cartel holds her wind-debt over her, and the jungle itself reclaims anyone who enters, forcing her through hostile growth.","arc":"Starts as a bitter, solitary guide who hides her guilt and refuses to share the route. When the jungle collapses a skybridge and Corvin's cable line is the only thing holding the party, she must hand him the anchor rope and trust him with a life. She ends as a guide who shares leadership and forgives herself, leading everyone out together.","personality_traits":["sardonic","resourceful","guarded","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pathfinding","description":"Reads wind currents and vine growth to find safe routes through shifting terrain.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cable Rigging","description":"Quickly braids and anchors cloudstone cable to cross gaps.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_hale","name":"Corvin Hale","role":"supporting","description":"A young Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, lanky and soot-stained, with singed eyebrows and a satchel of braiding tools. He joined the expedition to inspect the ruined skybridge anchors that tie the lost city to the network.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"He wants to prove the Wardens' craft can reconnect forgotten isles and earn his master's rank.","goal":"Survey and repair the ancient anchor-bridge at the lost city.","flaw":"He is reckless and follows rules to the letter even when the situation demands improvisation.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between loyalty to the Wardens' rigid code and his instinct to take risks that actually save people.","external_conflict":"The Toll War makes the Cartel treat Wardens as enemies, and Cartel-aligned Maren and Isolde obstruct his work.","arc":"Begins as a rule-bound apprentice who recites regulations to avoid decisions. When Maren hands him the anchor rope on the collapsing bridge, he abandons protocol and improvises a knot that saves the party. He ends as a confident engineer who trusts his judgment alongside the code.","personality_traits":["earnest","eager","nervous","clever"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone cable under pressure.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_crane","name":"Isolde Crane","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished Drift Cartel factor in her fifties, with silver-threaded rings and a calm, courteous voice. She finances the expedition and travels with it, intending to claim whatever the lost city holds for the Cartel.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"She wants the lost city's hidden trade routes to cement Cartel control over all inter-isle shipping.","goal":"Seize the city's cartographic and cloudstone secrets before the Wardens or Silverspine can.","flaw":"Her greed makes her treat people as ledger entries and ignore warnings of danger.","internal_conflict":"She fears the Cartel will discard her if she fails, yet she despises how far she has sacrificed her own principles.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and Grain Levy leave her opposed by Wardens and the Hollow Circle, and the jungle punishes her recklessness.","arc":"Starts as a controlled patron certain she can buy any outcome. When the jungle drags away her hired porters after she orders a shortcut Maren warned against, she faces the cost of her greed. She ends stripped of her cargo, either abandoning her claim to save others or being claimed by the ruins.","personality_traits":["calculating","polite","ruthless","image-conscious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt contracts to bind and coerce others.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","description":"A cheerful, round-faced cartographer from Silverspine Academy, with ink-stained fingers and spectacles patched with wire. He wants to chart the lost city and map the jungle's changing growth.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","motivation":"He wants to be the first scholar to map a lost isle, earning a chair at the Academy.","goal":"Produce a complete map of the ruins and the skybridge routes leading to them.","flaw":"His curiosity makes him wander off and ignore danger and orders.","internal_conflict":"He is afraid his scholarship is merely derivative and that he has never done anything original.","external_conflict":"Isolde wants his maps for the Cartel, and the jungle keeps altering the terrain he charts.","arc":"Begins as an eager scholar who treats the ruins as an academic puzzle. After wandering off and being trapped by shifting vines, he is rescued only because Maren follows his chalk marks, realizing his habit endangers others. He ends as a careful mapmaker who refuses to sell his map to the Cartel and shares it with the Academy.","personality_traits":["curious","chatty","absent-minded","kind"],"abilities":[{"name":"Terrain Charting","description":"Rapidly sketches accurate maps of unfamiliar landscapes.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_isolde_debt","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Crane holds Maren Voss's wind-debt and uses it to force her to guide the expedition, creating constant resentment between them."},{"id":"rel_isolde_maren_control","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Crane distrusts Maren Voss's caution and tries to override her route decisions, pushing the expedition into danger."},{"id":"rel_corvin_maren_trust","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Corvin Hale looks up to Maren Voss as a veteran guide, and their growing trust tests her refusal to rely on others."},{"id":"rel_tobias_isolde_maps","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Wren is pressured by Isolde Crane to hand over his maps for the Cartel, conflicting with his loyalty to the Academy."},{"id":"rel_maren_tobias_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Voss reluctantly protects Tobias Wren and teaches him to follow jungle discipline, reminding her of her lost party."}]}
