{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_valeria_corvane","name":"Valeria Corvane","description":"A former senator of the Aetherian assembly, now in her fifties, stripped of her seat after a bridge-tax scandal she was framed for. She is gaunt and grey-streaked, wears a plain ash-coloured mantle, and lives in quiet exile at Silverspine Academy, where she studies old skybridge charts and the assembly's precedents.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To restore her family's name by proving the demagogue's rise was built on fraud and manipulated wind-debts.","goal":"Expose Aurelian Voss before the senate votes to give him emergency powers over every skybridge toll.","flaw":"Her pride makes her treat allies as instruments and conceal her plans from them.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between lawful reform and the temptation to destroy Voss by methods she once condemned.","external_conflict":"She is barred from the senate floor and hunted by Cartel agents who profit from Voss's rise.","arc":"Starts as a proud, secretive exile who manipulates others. Her pivotal choice comes when she can sabotage a skybridge cable at Emberroost to discredit Voss, but would strand the Hollow's grain shipments. She refuses, openly confides in Ilyra and Tobren, and ends as a humbler leader who wins through shared testimony instead of deceit.","personality_traits":["calculating","proud","weary","disciplined"],"abilities":[{"name":"Parliamentary Strategy","description":"Knows senate procedure and precedent well enough to turn rules into weapons.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Chart Reading","description":"Reads skybridge charts to predict where wind-debt pressure and tolls will fall.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_aurelian_voss","name":"Aurelian Voss","description":"A charismatic populist orator in his forties who rose from the docks of Mistral Docks, with a broad frame, a warm voice and a scar across his jaw. He promises to cancel every citizen's wind-debt and funds his rallies through the Drift Cartel.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To seize lasting power so no one can ever again hold his dock-born family in debt.","goal":"Win emergency authority over the skybridge tolls and the senate's grain levy.","flaw":"He cannot tolerate dissent and mistakes the crowd's applause for proof he is right.","internal_conflict":"He half-believes his own promises while knowing the Cartel deals behind them betray the poor.","external_conflict":"Valeria's investigation and the Hollow Circle's refusal of the grain levy threaten his rise.","arc":"Starts as a sincere champion of the indebted who is already compromised by Cartel money. The pivotal moment comes when the Hollow Circle refuses the grain levy and he orders its mills seized. He crosses fully into tyranny, and his public fall comes when his own dockworkers see the order.","personality_traits":["charismatic","paranoid","ambitious","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crowd Oratory","description":"Moves large assemblies with simple, emotional rhetoric.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ilyra_denn","name":"Ilyra Denn","description":"A young Bridge Warden engineer of about twenty-six at Emberroost, soot-stained and wiry, with calloused hands and braided cable-cord in her hair. She keeps a private ledger of tolls that do not match the Cartel's published figures.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe from tolls that starve their maintenance.","goal":"Get her ledger of falsified tolls into the senate record.","flaw":"She is impulsive and acts on anger before she checks the facts.","internal_conflict":"She is loyal to the Wardens but suspects her superiors take Cartel bribes.","external_conflict":"Her superiors order her to stop auditing the tolls, and Cartel enforcers watch the forge-pits.","arc":"Starts as an angry junior engineer who acts rashly. Her pivotal moment comes when she nearly lights an open flame near a cable to protest, breaking the no-fire rule, and Valeria stops her. She learns to wait and verify, and ends by testifying carefully before the senate.","personality_traits":["fiery","skilled","loyal","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone cables faster than most Wardens.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_tobren_hale","name":"Tobren Hale","description":"An elder miller of the Hollow Circle in his sixties, broad-shouldered and slow-spoken, with flour-dusted sleeves. He remembers the Great Calm from stories told by his grandmother and distrusts every city politician.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's farmers from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Secure a senate ruling that voids the grain levy.","flaw":"He distrusts outsiders so deeply that he refuses help that could save his people.","internal_conflict":"He values the Circle's quiet independence but sees that only open politics can save it.","external_conflict":"Voss's agents threaten to seize the mills if the levy goes unpaid.","arc":"Starts as a stubborn isolationist who refuses to deal with the senate. His pivotal choice comes when Voss's agents threaten his mills and Valeria offers a joint petition. He accepts, and ends as the Circle's public voice in the capital.","personality_traits":["stubborn","patient","wise","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Lore","description":"Judges harvest yields and mill output from a single handful of grain.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_cassia_marl","name":"Cassia Marl","description":"A sharp-eyed Drift Cartel factor in her late thirties, stationed at Mistral Docks, in embroidered grey silks. She manages Voss's funding and is privately weighing her loyalties.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the Cartel profitable and herself safe from Voss's growing volatility.","goal":"Secure a stable shipping-lane monopoly without a collapse of the toll system.","flaw":"She treats every loyalty as a transaction and so trusts no one.","internal_conflict":"She is unsure whether to stay with Voss or sell him out to protect the Cartel.","external_conflict":"Voss's purges threaten Cartel factors, and Valeria's inquiries threaten her accounts.","arc":"Starts as a calculating fixer who serves Voss. Her pivotal moment comes when Voss orders the Hollow mills seized and ruins the Cartel's grain supply. She secretly gives Valeria her account books, and ends as an uneasy turncoat who accepts the cost of honesty.","personality_traits":["pragmatic","cunning","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Craft","description":"Hides and traces money through shipping manifests and wind-debt records.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_valeria_voss_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_aurelian_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Valeria Corvane is sworn to bring down Aurelian Voss, whose rise she blames for her disgrace, while Voss sees her as the last credible threat to his power."},{"id":"rel_valeria_ilyra_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_ilyra_denn","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Valeria Corvane guides Ilyra Denn's toll evidence toward the senate, but her secrecy risks Ilyra's trust and safety."},{"id":"rel_tobren_valeria_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tobren_hale","target_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobren Hale reluctantly joins Valeria Corvane against the grain levy, but he suspects her of being another politician using the Hollow."},{"id":"rel_cassia_voss_ally","source_character_id":"chr_cassia_marl","target_character_id":"chr_aurelian_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Cassia Marl funds and manages Aurelian Voss for the Cartel, a tie that turns to resentment as his purges grow."},{"id":"rel_cassia_valeria_rival","source_character_id":"chr_cassia_marl","target_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Cassia Marl tracks Valeria Corvane's investigation, and later becomes a hidden source for her."}]}
