{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kael_voss","name":"Kael Voss","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered wayfarer in her late thirties, Kael grew up among the Hollow Circle's windmills before leaving to walk the glass wastes that ring the drifting isles. She is lean and sun-scorched, with a cloudstone-cord bracelet she never removes and a coat patched with sailcloth. She speaks little and carries almost nothing.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To outrun the memory of the grain shipment she failed to protect, which ruined her village's season.","goal":"Cross the glass desert and reach the far edge where the wind-debt ledgers say a stranded debt-holder waits.","flaw":"She refuses all help, mistaking isolation for strength.","internal_conflict":"She longs to belong again but believes she forfeited that right when the Cartel levy took her people's grain.","external_conflict":"She carries an unpaid wind-debt, and Cartel collectors are tracking her across the glass.","arc":"Kael begins as a silent loner who treats every offered hand as a debt. When Dorran Pell, the collector hunting her, is stranded by a glass storm, she must choose between leaving him to die or sharing her last water, and she shares it. She ends the journey willing to accept aid and repay her debt in labour at Mistral Docks rather than flee it.","personality_traits":["taciturn","stubborn","observant","resourceful","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Glass-reading","description":"She can judge the stability of glass dunes by their colour and sound.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Windmill mending","description":"She can repair mechanical gears with improvised tools.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_dorran_pell","name":"Dorran Pell","role":"antagonist","description":"A broad, soft-spoken debt collector in his fifties, employed by the Drift Cartel at Mistral Docks. He wears a salt-stained grey coat and carries a brass ledger. Years of hauling debts across the isles have made him methodical rather than cruel.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a promotion that would let him retire from the road and pay for his sister's care.","goal":"Bring Kael back to Mistral Docks to settle her wind-debt in full.","flaw":"He treats every person as a column of figures, ignoring their circumstances.","internal_conflict":"He suspects the Cartel's levies are unjust but depends on its pay.","external_conflict":"He must cross the dangerous glass desert on foot, a terrain he is unprepared for, while the Cartel's patience runs short.","arc":"Dorran starts as a rigid enforcer who trusts the ledger over people. Stranded by a glass storm, he is saved by Kael's water, and the debt he owes her breaks his rule that debts are only measured in goods. He ends by striking her debt from his ledger and reporting the Cartel's levy practices to the Bridge Wardens.","personality_traits":["methodical","patient","weary","polite"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt appraisal","description":"He can quickly estimate what a person owes and can pay.","category":"social"},{"name":"Tracking","description":"He follows trails by reading small traces left behind.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_marrow","name":"Isolde Marrow","role":"supporting","description":"An elderly cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained hands and sharp grey eyes. She once mapped skybridge routes and now charts the glass desert from reports. She gives Kael her only map.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To complete the first full chart of the glass desert before her sight fails.","goal":"Obtain firsthand measurements of the desert's far edge through Kael's journey.","flaw":"She values her maps above the safety of those who gather data for her.","internal_conflict":"She knows she is sending a traveller into danger for her own legacy.","external_conflict":"The Academy board refuses to fund desert surveys, leaving her reliant on secret favours.","arc":"Isolde begins as a detached scholar who treats travellers as instruments. When Kael's returning report shows her chart has a fatal error that would have killed later travellers, Isolde publicly corrects her map, crediting Kael. She ends by prioritising traveller safety over her reputation.","personality_traits":["exacting","curious","proud","dry-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cartography","description":"She can reconstruct routes from fragmentary reports.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_dorran_hunts_kael","source_character_id":"chr_dorran_pell","target_character_id":"chr_kael_voss","relationship_type":"pursuer","description":"Dorran Pell is the Drift Cartel collector pursuing Kael Voss across the glass desert to enforce her unpaid wind-debt, creating constant pressure on her journey."},{"id":"rel_kael_distrusts_dorran","source_character_id":"chr_kael_voss","target_character_id":"chr_dorran_pell","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Kael Voss distrusts and evades Dorran Pell, seeing him as the face of the Cartel levy that ruined her village, until she saves his life."},{"id":"rel_isolde_equips_kael","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_kael_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Isolde Marrow supplies Kael Voss with a map of the glass desert, but her need for data pressures Kael to take a riskier route than she would choose."}]}
