{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kaelen_vorr","name":"Kaelen Vorr","description":"A lean, sun-weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her late thirties, raised in the cable-braiding sheds of Emberroost. Her palms are scarred from cloudstone fibres, and she wears a soot-grey coat stitched with the wardens' knotted-rope sigil. She inherited her mother's post as Chief Braider after the Toll War cost the Wardens half their crews.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges intact so the isles never fall into isolation, as her mother's crew once feared during the Great Calm stories she grew up on.","goal":"Forge a three-isle alliance that funds bridge repair and stands against the common enemy threatening the archipelago.","flaw":"Rigid pride in craft; she dismisses merchants and farmers as people who do not understand the stakes.","internal_conflict":"She longs to protect the bridges at any cost but fears that her uncompromising stance is what keeps the isles divided.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's toll hikes starve her crews of labour and goods while the wind-debt keeps accruing against Emberroost.","arc":"Kaelen begins as a proud engineer who refuses to share bridge-command with merchants. When a Cartel tollkeeper's refusal to let a repair crew cross leaves a skybridge fraying, she is forced to accept Dorian's offer of Cartel ships and wind-debt forgiveness. She ends as a negotiator who treats the other factions as partners and shares control of the bridge network.","personality_traits":["proud","meticulous","stubborn","loyal","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Reads tension in cloudstone cable by touch and braids repairs that hold under storm load.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Shielded Forge Lore","description":"Knows how to work inside shielded forge-pits safely, honouring the ban on open flame aloft.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_dorian_pell","name":"Dorian Pell","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel factor in his fifties, stout and immaculately dressed in wind-silk with rings stamped with Cartel seals. He rose from deckhand to ledger-keeper at Mistral Docks and now manages the shipping lanes the Cartel charter guarantees.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's long-term profit by making sure the lanes survive the common enemy's assault.","goal":"Broker a binding treaty that preserves Cartel lane monopolies while committing Cartel ships to the war effort.","flaw":"Treats every relationship as a transaction and cannot offer anything without counting the return.","internal_conflict":"He privately admires the Wardens' craft and the Hollow's honesty but believes sentiment is what bankrupts houses.","external_conflict":"Cartel princes above him demand he press the grain levy, which threatens to break the alliance he is building.","arc":"Dorian starts as a ledger-minded broker who uses the Grain Levy as leverage over Marta. When the levy causes a Hollow mill-stop that starves Mistral Docks' crews, he sees the cost of his transactions and chooses to suspend it against Cartel orders. He ends as a trusted guarantor who has sacrificed profit for the alliance.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","pragmatic","secretly sentimental"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Brokerage","description":"Negotiates shipping rights and debt settlements that bind merchants and captains.","category":"social"},{"name":"Wind-Debt Accounting","description":"Tracks wind-debt across isles and knows how to restructure it.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_marta_oakhand","name":"Marta Oakhand","description":"A broad-shouldered Hollow Circle miller in her mid-forties with flour-dusted forearms and a braid of greying wheat-gold hair. She leads the windmill cooperatives of The Hollow, a role she took on after surviving the Great Calm tales told by her grandparents of hunger and self-reliance.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and her people free of debts they never chose.","goal":"Win an end to the Grain Levy as the price of Hollow Circle support in the alliance.","flaw":"Distrust born of long exploitation makes her reject help even when it is sincerely offered.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect her people by staying out of the war yet knows isolation is what made the Great Calm so deadly.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy drains her stores while the common enemy threatens the mills' wind supply.","arc":"Marta starts by refusing every offer from outsiders and withholding grain. After Kaelen's crew repairs the skybridge to The Hollow at their own wind-debt cost, she chooses to open the granaries to the allied armies. She ends as the alliance's quartermaster who accepts mutual dependence.","personality_traits":["steadfast","wary","generous with her own","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Mastery","description":"Reads wind patterns and keeps mills grinding through shifting currents.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Community Rallying","description":"Organizes dispersed farm cooperatives to act together.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_thane","name":"Isolde Thane","description":"A sharp-eyed cartographer at Silverspine Academy in her late twenties, ink-stained and always carrying rolled charts. A Bridge Warden affiliate, she maps the ever-shifting skybridge network and was the first to notice a pattern in the enemy's attacks.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove her theory that the isles are safest if the skybridges are cut and each isle stands alone.","goal":"Sever the key skybridges between the three cities before the alliance can be sealed.","flaw":"Certainty: she trusts her calculations over people and will not revise them.","internal_conflict":"She loves the beauty of the bridge network she charts yet believes it is the enemy's road to conquest.","external_conflict":"Kaelen's alliance depends on the very bridges she wants cut, and the Wardens' leadership has ordered her silent.","arc":"Isolde begins as an academic dissenter who hoards her findings. When Kaelen shows her the Great Calm records at Silverspine proving isolation starved the isles, she weighs her model against them and chooses to publish her maps to the allies instead of sabotaging the bridges. She ends as the alliance's cartographer, correcting her own flawed model.","personality_traits":["brilliant","aloof","obsessive","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drift patterns and predicts bridge failure points.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Spark Sabotage Knowledge","description":"Knows exactly where a single spark would sever a bridge, given the ban on open flame aloft.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kaelen_dorian_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_kaelen_vorr","target_character_id":"chr_dorian_pell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Kaelen Vorr resents Dorian Pell for the Cartel tolls that choke her Warden crews, and Dorian sees Kaelen's rigidity as a threat to Cartel lanes, so every negotiation between them starts as a standoff."},{"id":"rel_marta_dorian_adversary","source_character_id":"chr_marta_oakhand","target_character_id":"chr_dorian_pell","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Marta Oakhand blames Dorian Pell for enforcing the Grain Levy on the Hollow Circle, and her refusal to supply the alliance is aimed squarely at him."},{"id":"rel_kaelen_marta_ally","source_character_id":"chr_kaelen_vorr","target_character_id":"chr_marta_oakhand","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kaelen Vorr repairs the Hollow's skybridge for Marta Oakhand at her own crew's cost, building a fragile trust that makes Marta's later grain commitment possible."},{"id":"rel_isolde_kaelen_foe","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_thane","target_character_id":"chr_kaelen_vorr","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Thane, a fellow Warden, plots to cut the skybridges that Kaelen Vorr is trying to preserve, turning a shared faction into a bitter ideological rift."},{"id":"rel_dorian_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_dorian_pell","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_thane","relationship_type":"patron","description":"Dorian Pell secretly funds Isolde Thane's survey work to gain advance knowledge of bridge failures, which makes him complicit in her sabotage plans and a hidden pressure on the alliance."}]}
