aw":"Timid under authority; she withholds findings that implicate powerful people.","internal_conflict":"She wants academic neutrality but feels complicit in the attack's consequences because her warning went unpublished.","external_conflict":"Academy elders, pressed by Cartel patrons, ask her to suppress her charts.","arc":"Starts as a hesitant scholar sitting on a damning chart. After Mara's crews are stranded because of the suppressed warning, she publishes the chart at Silverspine's public assembly. She ends as a confident advocate who stands behind her data.","personality_traits":["curious","anxious","precise","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift charting","description":"Predicts island and skybridge movement from wind records.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_oakhand","name":"Bram Oakhand","role":"supporting","description":"A 45-year-old miller and elder of the Hollow Circle, thick-armed and sunburnt, with flour-dusted hair. His windmills feed half the archipelago, and his grain barges depend on the skybridges.","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","motivation":"To keep the isles fed and his community free of Cartel debt.","goal":"Secure a repeal of the Grain Levy by allying with the Wardens during the rebuilding.","flaw":"Stubborn distrust of outsiders that makes him refuse compromise.","internal_conflict":"He values the Hollow's quiet self-reliance from the Great Calm yet knows isolation will starve them without the bridges.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy squeezes the Hollow, and the collapse blocks grain shipments.","arc":"Starts as an isolationist who refuses to send help. When the grain stores run low during the blockade and Mara asks for volunteer braiders, he sends Hollow workers to Emberroost. He ends as a bridge between the farming isle and the Wardens.","personality_traits":["stubborn","generous","weathered","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community leadership","description":"Rallies Hollow fa