me":"Teodor Hale","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"A 52-year-old miller turned mine foreman who left The Hollow after the Grain Levy ruined his mill. He is broad, gentle-voiced, with flour-pale scarring on his hands and a habit of humming windmill rhythms. He discovered the dreamstone in a collapsed shaft.","personality_traits":["warm","protective","sentimental"],"motivation":"To keep his crew together and fed after losing his family's mill.","goal":"Protect the dreamstone as the colony's source of comfort and income.","flaw":"Clings to comforting illusions and avoids confronting loss.","internal_conflict":"He loves the dreams where his mill still runs but knows the crew is wasting away asleep.","external_conflict":"Maren's investigation threatens to shut the stone, while the Cartel pressures him to ship it.","arc":"Begins as a devoted guardian of the stone who hides signs of sickness among his crew. After watching a young miner collapse during a shared dream, he must decide whether to side with Maren against the Cartel's buyers. He smashes his own stash of fragments and ends as a man willing to grieve his mill honestly.","abilities":[{"name":"Crew Leadership","description":"Rallies miners with calm authority.","category":"social"},{"name":"Grain Sense","description":"Reads winds and weather from long years at the windmills.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_crane","name":"Isolde Crane","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"A 45-year-old Cartel factor in immaculate indigo coats, with silver rings on each finger and a smile that never reaches her eyes. She rose from dockhand to merchant princess through the Toll War and now eyes the dreamstone as the ultimate trade good.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","patient","ruthless"],"motivation":"To secure permanent Cartel control over a commodity no rival can match.","goal":"Ship dreamstone shards to every isle and bind buyers into wind-debt.","flaw":"Believes every person has a price, so cannot read sincerity.","internal_conflict":"She secretly sleeps beside a shard to dream of the docks she grew up on and fears she is addicted.","external_conflict":"The Bridge Wardens and the Hollow Circle both oppose her, and Maren's report could halt the trade.","arc":"Starts as a confident profiteer insisting the stone is harmless. When a shard shipment causes a dock crew to sleepwalk off Mistral Docks, she is forced to choose between burying the report and losing her own dream. She doubles down and ends exposed and isolated as the Cartel disowns her.","abilities":[{"name":"Debt Weaving","description":"Turns wind-debts into leverage over rivals.","category":"social"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Reads desires and closes deals under pressure.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_ardent","name":"Pell Ardent","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A 22-year-old cartographer's apprentice with ink-stained fingers, cropped red hair, and thick spectacles. He maps shifting skybridges at Silverspine Academy and was assigned to chart the dream field's reach.","personality_traits":["curious","anxious","earnest"],"motivation":"To prove himself as a true cartographer and escape his mentor's shadow.","goal":"Map the dream field to show exactly which isles it reaches.","flaw":"Reckless curiosity makes him ignore warnings.","internal_conflict":"He fears he is merely a copyist, yet the stone's dreams show him maps he never drew.","external_conflict":"Wardens order him to stop mapping, and the Cartel bribes him for his charts.","arc":"Starts as an eager apprentice who ignores Maren's cautions. When his own sleepwalking nearly sends him over a skybridge rail, rescued by Maren, he accepts her discipline. He ends by publishing an honest chart crediting his own careful work.","abilities":[{"name":"Cartography","description":"Draws precise maps of drifting isles and bridges.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Dream Mapping","description":"Sketches landscapes seen in shared dreams.","category":"supernatural"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_isolde_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maren Voss opposes Isolde Crane, whose Cartel profits depend on suppressing Maren's Warden report about the dreamstone, echoing the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_isolde_teodor_leverage","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_crane","target_character_id":"chr_teodor_hale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Crane pressures Teodor Hale by using the Grain Levy debts that ruined his mill to force him to ship dreamstone."},{"id":"rel_teodor_maren_wary","source_character_id":"chr_teodor_hale","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Teodor Hale distrusts Maren Voss as a threat to the stone he protects, yet slowly sees she shares his care for people."},{"id":"rel_maren_pell_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_pell_ardent","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Maren Voss reluctantly mentors Pell Ardent, a fellow Warden whose recklessness reminds her of her father's last season."}]}
