{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_veln","name":"Mara Veln","description":"A lean, sun-weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her early thirties, with rope-scarred hands and a coil of cloudstone cable always slung over one shoulder. Raised in the forge-island of Emberroost, she apprenticed under the cable-braiders and rose quickly after inspecting skybridge joints that others feared to cross. Her cropped copper hair is singed at the ends from forge-pit work.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe after watching a frayed span drop a family of travelers into the clouds when she was a girl.","goal":"Secure enough funding and cloudstone to reinforce the three most overloaded skybridges before the next storm season.","flaw":"Stubborn perfectionism that makes her refuse help and delay decisions until every detail is certain.","internal_conflict":"She believes safety demands absolute control, yet she knows the network is too vast for one person to guarantee.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls in the Toll War choke the Wardens' funding and pressure her to approve cheaper, riskier repairs.","arc":"Mara begins as a lone perfectionist who inspects every span herself and trusts no one. When the Toll War forces a crisis and a Cartel-linked span begins to fail, she must choose between waiting for a flawless fix and trusting Tobren's crew to help her reinforce it in a single night. She chooses to delegate and share control, ending as a leader who builds a trained corps of inspectors rather than a solitary guardian.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","protective","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and splicing cloudstone cable to restore damaged skybridge spans.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Tension Sense","description":"Can judge a bridge's strain by feel and sound underfoot.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_tobren_hask","name":"Tobren Hask","description":"A broad-shouldered, charming Drift Cartel factor in his forties, always dressed in a wind-faded teal coat stitched with the Cartel's sigil. Born to a poor dockhand family at Mistral Docks, he clawed his way up through shipping ledgers and favors. He keeps a polished brass toll-token he turns over in his fingers when negotiating.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To never again be poor or powerless as he was growing up on the docks.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and win exclusive shipping rights over the Hollow's grain routes for the Cartel.","flaw":"Greed disguised as pragmatism, which blinds him to the human cost of his deals.","internal_conflict":"He privately resents the Cartel princes who treat him as disposable, yet he depends on their approval for his status.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his levies and tolls in the Toll War and the Grain Levy.","arc":"Tobren starts as a confident enforcer of Cartel tolls who sees ruin as the price of order. When the Grain Levy sparks a famine threat and the Cartel princes blame him, he is cast aside by his own faction. Humbled, he trades his ledgers to Mara as evidence of illegal tolls, ending as a reluctant ally who breaks his dependence on the Cartel's approval.","personality_traits":["charismatic","calculating","insecure","persuasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks debts, tolls, and wind-debt obligations across dozens of isles from memory.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates tense deals and bends rivals toward his terms.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_pym","name":"Isolde Pym","description":"A soft-spoken cartographer at Silverspine Academy in her late twenties, with ink-stained fingers and spectacles tied to her head with a ribbon. She grew up among the Academy's map archives and charts the drifting skybridge network season by season. She carries rolled charts in a leather tube at all times.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To record the whole archipelago accurately so no traveler is ever lost to a miscalculated drift.","goal":"Complete a predictive map of skybridge drift patterns that can warn of failures before they happen.","flaw":"Cowardice about confrontation causes her to withhold uncomfortable findings.","internal_conflict":"She values truth in her charts but fears the political fallout of publishing data that implicates powerful factions.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents pressure the Academy to alter charts so favored routes appear safer and cheaper.","arc":"Isolde begins by quietly shelving data that shows Cartel-favored bridges are failing. After Mara shows her a collapsing span in the middle of the Toll War, she chooses to publish her predictive map publicly. She ends as a vocal truth-teller who stands behind her work despite the risk.","personality_traits":["gentle","observant","anxious","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Prediction","description":"Forecasts how isles and skybridges shift using layered seasonal charts.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_orrin_dale","name":"Orrin Dale","description":"A weathered, gray-bearded miller in his sixties from The Hollow, with flour-dusted forearms and a booming laugh. He has run the largest windmill on the isle for forty years and speaks for the Hollow Circle. His mill's sails are patched with scraps from every harvest he has survived.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the Hollow's farmers and their grain from being squeezed by outside merchants, as they were during the Great Calm.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's grain levy and establish a fair shipping arrangement for Hollow harvests.","flaw":"Pride and distrust of outsiders makes him reject compromises that could actually help.","internal_conflict":"He wants his community to thrive but fears that any cooperation with other factions betrays the self-reliance the Great Calm taught them.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's Grain Levy threatens to bankrupt the Hollow's farmers and starve the isles that depend on them.","arc":"Orrin begins by refusing every offer of help from the Wardens, convinced the Hollow must stand alone as it did in the Great Calm. When the levy leaves the granaries nearly empty, he accepts Mara's offer to have Warden bridges carry grain outside Cartel lanes. He ends by joining a shared alliance against the tolls.","personality_traits":["proud","warm","stubborn","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Lore","description":"Reads wind and soil to predict harvests and manage reserves through lean seasons.","category":"other"},{"name":"Community Authority","description":"Commands deep respect among Hollow farmers and can rally them quickly.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobren_toll_rivals","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_tobren_hask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Veln and Tobren Hask are rivals in the Toll War: his rising tolls starve her Wardens of funds, while her safety demands expose the cost-cutting behind his deals."},{"id":"rel_tobren_orrin_levy_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_tobren_hask","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_dale","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Tobren Hask enforces the Cartel's grain levy against Orrin Dale, who refuses to pay and rallies the Hollow farmers against him."},{"id":"rel_mara_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_pym","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Mara Veln mentors Isolde Pym in reading field conditions on skybridges, pressing her to publish the drift data that threatens Cartel interests."},{"id":"rel_orrin_mara_wary_ally","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_dale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orrin Dale is a wary ally of Mara Veln: he distrusts outsiders but needs her Warden bridges to move grain beyond Cartel shipping lanes."}]}
