sive action until it is nearly too late.","internal_conflict":"He wants peace for his community but suspects that peace alone will let the Cartel starve them.","external_conflict":"Cartel collectors arrive each season demanding grain that his community cannot spare.","arc":"Tobias begins as a hesitant miller who hopes the levy will fade away. When Cartel collectors seize a season's grain, he decides to stop waiting and agrees to back Mara's evidence with the Hollow Circle's testimony. He ends as a confident community leader willing to confront the Cartel.","personality_traits":["gentle","patient","cautious","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"He keeps mills running and repairs them with improvised parts.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_quill","name":"Ilse Quill","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, barely twenty-five, with ink-stained fingers, round spectacles, and a satchel overflowing with charts. Born to a Mistral Docks shipping family, she left to study the skybridge network.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful mapping can protect people better than force or money.","goal":"Complete an accurate chart of the shifting skybridge network that exposes where cables have been tampered with.","flaw":"Naive and overconfident in data; she ignores political danger around her findings.","internal_conflict":"She feels guilty that her family's shipping business profits from the tolls she is learning to oppose.","external_conflict":"Her academy superiors, pressured by Cartel patrons, try to suppress her charts.","arc":"Ilse starts as a naive scholar who believes facts speak for themselves. When her charts are confiscated after revealing suspicious cable failures, she chooses to give copies to Mara and defy her family. She ends as a politically aware ally who understands that truth needs protectors.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","bookish","brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"She charts drifting bridge routes and predicts shifts in the network.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Veln blames Corvin Ashgrave's toll schemes for the cable failures that killed her brother and hunts for proof against him."},{"id":"rel_corvin_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Ashgrave views Mara Veln as a dangerous inspector and works to discredit her and bury her evidence."},{"id":"rel_ilse_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilse Quill supplies Mara Veln with charts of suspicious cable failures, while Mara teaches her to survive the politics around her findings."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Wren resists Corvin Ashgrave's Grain Levy on behalf of the Hollow Circle, and Corvin tries to bully him into compliance."},{"id":"rel_mara_tobias_ally","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Veln and Tobias Wren join forces against the Drift Cartel, with Mara pushing Tobias to act and Tobias softening her abrasiveness."}]}
