{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_veln","name":"Mara Veln","description":"A wiry Bridge Warden inspector in her thirties, with soot-stained gloves, a braided cloudstone cord worn at her wrist, and a permanent squint from years of watching cables sway. Raised in the forge-pits of Emberroost, she trained as a cable-braider before taking up inspection work, and she speaks in dry, cutting asides.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe after watching a frayed cable kill her brother during a crossing.","goal":"Prove that the Drift Cartel has been sabotaging bridge cables to justify higher tolls.","flaw":"Sardonic and abrasive; she mocks allies and alienates people who could help her.","internal_conflict":"She distrusts authority yet depends on the Wardens' rigid code to feel her brother's death meant something.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves her outgunned against Cartel lawyers and enforcers who bury her evidence.","arc":"Mara begins as a lone, caustic inspector who trusts no one. When she discovers a tampered cable on the skybridge to Silverspine during the Toll War, she must choose between using the evidence alone to seek revenge or sharing it with the Hollow Circle and the Wardens openly. She chooses to share it, ending as a coalition-builder who replaces sarcasm with trust.","personality_traits":["sardonic","stubborn","observant","loyal","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"She can tell a cable's age and tampering by touch and sound.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Forensic Eye","description":"She pieces together how a bridge failure happened from small physical clues.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","name":"Corvin Ashgrave","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties, with rings on every finger, a tailored coat of dyed sailcloth, and a smile that never reaches his eyes. He rose from dockhand to ledger-master at Mistral Docks and now runs the toll schedules.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure a lasting fortune and never again be poor like the dockhand he once was.","goal":"Raise skybridge tolls and force the Grain Levy through so the Cartel owns every supply line.","flaw":"Greed that makes him cut corners and underestimate people he considers beneath him.","internal_conflict":"He despises the debts that bind others, yet he is quietly terrified of his own origins being exposed.","external_conflict":"The Wardens' inspections and the Hollow Circle's resistance threaten his toll and levy schemes.","arc":"Corvin starts as a confident, untouchable toll-master. When Mara's evidence of cable tampering surfaces and his own partners abandon him, he is forced to choose between fleeing or confessing. He tries to flee, is stripped of his charter privileges, and ends ruined but briefly honest about the poverty that drove him.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"He negotiates people into deals that quietly favour him.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Mastery","description":"He tracks wind-debt and shipments across the whole archipelago in his head.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","description":"A soft-spoken miller of the Hollow Circle in his forties, broad-shouldered with flour-dusted forearms and a weathered straw hat. He has worked the windmills of The Hollow since childhood and quietly organises neighbours against the Cartel levy.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the farmers who survived the Great Calm by relying on each other.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's grain levy without sparking open violence on his island.","flaw":"Conflict-averse; he delays decisive action until it is nearly too late.","internal_conflict":"He wants peace for his community but suspects that peace alone will let the Cartel starve them.","external_conflict":"Cartel collectors arrive each season demanding grain that his community cannot spare.","arc":"Tobias begins as a hesitant miller who hopes the levy will fade away. When Cartel collectors seize a season's grain, he decides to stop waiting and agrees to back Mara's evidence with the Hollow Circle's testimony. He ends as a confident community leader willing to confront the Cartel.","personality_traits":["gentle","patient","cautious","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"He keeps mills running and repairs them with improvised parts.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_quill","name":"Ilse Quill","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, barely twenty-five, with ink-stained fingers, round spectacles, and a satchel overflowing with charts. Born to a Mistral Docks shipping family, she left to study the skybridge network.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful mapping can protect people better than force or money.","goal":"Complete an accurate chart of the shifting skybridge network that exposes where cables have been tampered with.","flaw":"Naive and overconfident in data; she ignores political danger around her findings.","internal_conflict":"She feels guilty that her family's shipping business profits from the tolls she is learning to oppose.","external_conflict":"Her academy superiors, pressured by Cartel patrons, try to suppress her charts.","arc":"Ilse starts as a naive scholar who believes facts speak for themselves. When her charts are confiscated after revealing suspicious cable failures, she chooses to give copies to Mara and defy her family. She ends as a politically aware ally who understands that truth needs protectors.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","bookish","brave"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"She charts drifting bridge routes and predicts shifts in the network.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Veln blames Corvin Ashgrave's toll schemes for the cable failures that killed her brother and hunts for proof against him."},{"id":"rel_corvin_mara_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Ashgrave views Mara Veln as a dangerous inspector and works to discredit her and bury her evidence."},{"id":"rel_ilse_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ilse Quill supplies Mara Veln with charts of suspicious cable failures, while Mara teaches her to survive the politics around her findings."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_ashgrave","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Wren resists Corvin Ashgrave's Grain Levy on behalf of the Hollow Circle, and Corvin tries to bully him into compliance."},{"id":"rel_mara_tobias_ally","source_character_id":"chr_mara_veln","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Veln and Tobias Wren join forces against the Drift Cartel, with Mara pushing Tobias to act and Tobias softening her abrasiveness."}]}
