[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed rigger-turned-code-thief in her early thirties, born on Mistral Docks to a family of cargo haulers ruined by wind-debt. She learned to forge ledger entries and bridge-crossing tallies as a teenager and now sells her skill to anyone who can pay. Soot-stained gloves, a cropped silver-dyed haircut, and a coat lined with stolen cartel tally-slips mark her look.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To erase the crushing wind-debt that destroyed her family and to never owe anyone again.","goal":"Sell the stolen corporate AI seed for enough to buy out her family's debt ledger and vanish from the archipelago.","flaw":"Cynical self-interest: she assumes everyone has a price and refuses to rely on anyone.","internal_conflict":"She despises the Cartel's debt system yet profits from the same cynicism that sustains it.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel has named her the most wanted person in the archipelago and is hunting her across every skybridge.","arc":"Starts as a lone mercenary who trusts no one. After the Cartel burns her Mistral Docks safehouse and Tamsin Orrel shelters her at Silverspine, she chooses to release the AI seed's debt-erasing code publicly rather than sell it. She ends as an outlaw who accepts being owed and owing to allies, her cynicism tempered.","personality_traits":["cynical","resourceful","guarded","sardonic","quick-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Forgery","description":"Alters wind-debt records and crossing tallies so they pass inspection.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Dock Cant","description":"Fluent in smuggler slang and able to disappear into crowds at the port.","category":"social"},{"name":"Cloudstone Climbing","description":"Moves swiftly along cables and bridge scaffolds to avoid pursuit.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_dorian_marsh","name":"Dorian Marsh","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-tongued Cartel merchant prince in his fifties who oversaw the charter-era archives where the AI seed was kept. Heavyset, impeccably dressed in dyed sailcloth, with rings made from bridge-cable ends. He rose by turning every favor into a debt.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To keep the Cartel's monopoly over inter-isle trade and debt unbreakable, protecting the fortune he built.","goal":"Recover the AI seed and make an example of Kestrel Vane to deter future thieves.","flaw":"Hubris: he believes nothing escapes his ledgers, so he underestimates opponents.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears the seed could expose that his rise rested on falsified debts.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy and Toll War strain Cartel finances, and the theft threatens his standing with fellow princes.","arc":"Begins as a confident master of debt who treats the theft as a nuisance. When Kestrel leaks the seed's code and his falsified ledgers surface at Mistral Docks, he overreaches by ordering a toll blockade that turns the merchants against him. He ends stripped of authority, forced to face debts he cannot collect.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Knows whom to pressure through wind-debt obligations.","category":"social"},{"name":"Trade Network","description":"Commands informants and shipping crews across the lanes.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","name":"Tamsin Orrel","role":"supporting","description":"A middle-aged cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers and a cloak patched with old charts. A former Bridge Warden engineer, she left the field after a bridge failure killed her apprentice.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To expose the Cartel tolls that she believes neglected maintenance and caused her apprentice's death.","goal":"Use the AI seed to map and verify true bridge-maintenance costs, proving the tolls are fraudulent.","flaw":"Obsessive secrecy; she withholds plans from allies and acts alone.","internal_conflict":"Guilt over the failure tempts her to risk others to redeem herself.","external_conflict":"The Toll War pits the Wardens against the Cartel, and Silverspine's leadership fears reprisals if she shelters a fugitive.","arc":"Starts as a guilt-driven recluse hiding her research. When Cartel agents trace Kestrel to Silverspine, she chooses to publicly present her data to the Wardens rather than act alone. She ends as an open ally who shares the burden.","personality_traits":["meticulous","guilt-ridden","principled","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts shifting bridge networks and finds hidden routes.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Structural Insight","description":"Reads stress in cables and bridge designs.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_holloway","name":"Bram Holloway","role":"supporting","description":"A broad, soft-spoken miller from The Hollow with flour-dusted forearms, who runs a grain barge and quietly moves goods the Cartel would tax. He is respected by his neighbors.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect his community's grain from the Cartel levy and keep the isle fed.","goal":"Smuggle Kestrel off Mistral Docks in exchange for the seed's debt-erasing code freeing the Hollow Circle.","flaw":"Naive trust in neighbors makes him blind to informants.","internal_conflict":"Torn between his pacifist farming creed and the need to break rules to survive.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy leaves his barge and neighbors under constant Cartel inspection.","arc":"Begins as a cautious miller who avoids confrontation. After a Cartel inspector seizes his barge following a leak from a trusted neighbor, he organizes the Hollow Circle to run a coordinated grain convoy past the blockade. He ends as a leader who acts with vigilance rather than blind trust.","personality_traits":["gentle","loyal","trusting","steady"],"abilities":[{"name":"Barge Piloting","description":"Navigates cargo barges through crosswinds and storms.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Community Standing","description":"Neighbors across the Hollow follow his lead.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_marsh_hunts_vane","source_character_id":"chr_dorian_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Dorian Marsh hunts Kestrel Vane, the thief who stole the AI seed from his archives, and uses her family's old wind-debt as leverage against her."},{"id":"rel_vane_shelter_orrel","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kestrel Vane trades the AI seed's mapping data to Tamsin Orrel in return for shelter at Silverspine, though neither fully trusts the other."},{"id":"rel_orrel_defies_marsh","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","target_character_id":"chr_dorian_marsh","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Orrel opposes Dorian Marsh over Cartel tolls she blames for her apprentice's death, escalating the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_holloway_aids_vane","source_character_id":"chr_bram_holloway","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Bram Holloway offers Kestrel Vane passage on his grain barge, hoping her stolen code can free the Hollow Circle from the levy."},{"id":"rel_marsh_levies_holloway","source_character_id":"chr_dorian_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_bram_holloway","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Dorian Marsh enforces the Grain Levy against Bram Holloway and the Hollow Circle, inspecting his barge for contraband."}]}
</Output>
