{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_odalys_venn","name":"Odalys Venn","description":"A sharp-eyed retired Bridge Warden inspector in her late fifties, silver-haired and ink-stained, who wears a patched warden's coat everywhere. Having spent decades certifying skybridge cables at Silverspine, she now accepts weekend invitations to the manor as a quiet escape, and cannot resist untangling a puzzle.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To clear the name of the Wardens, whose cable inspections are about to be blamed for the host's death.","goal":"Identify the true killer before the skybridge back to the mainland is repaired and the guests disperse.","flaw":"Stubborn pride in her own deductions; she dismisses evidence that contradicts her first theory.","internal_conflict":"She fears her last signed inspection was flawed and that her retirement hides a career-ending mistake.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel guests push to pin the murder on the Wardens to justify higher tolls in the Toll War.","arc":"Begins certain the Cartel broker is guilty and guarding her reputation. When the cable ledger she trusts proves forged, she is forced to admit her own inspection error aloud before the guests. She ends humbler, naming the real killer through shared evidence rather than lone certainty.","personality_traits":["observant","stubborn","dry-witted","meticulous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"Can tell from a frayed strand of cloudstone how and when a rope was cut.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Patient Interrogation","description":"Draws out confessions through calm, repeated questioning.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_cassian_thorne","name":"Cassian Thorne","description":"A polished Drift Cartel broker in his forties with rings on every finger and a velvet coat dusted with dock grit. He holds the debts of several guests and arrives at the manor ostensibly to renegotiate shipping terms.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the host's signature on a monopoly deal that will make him a Cartel prince.","goal":"Hide the forged wind-debt ledgers that prove he has been inflating tolls.","flaw":"Greed that makes him reckless when a profit seems within reach.","internal_conflict":"He despises the cold merchant he has become but cannot give up the wealth that defines him.","external_conflict":"The victim had discovered the forged ledgers and threatened to expose them to the Wardens.","arc":"Starts as a confident schemer who believes money buries every problem. After the victim's death he panics and plants evidence against the Wardens, but Odalys's ledger comparison traps him. He ends exposed and stripped of his Cartel standing, forced to face what his greed has cost.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Talks guests into favourable terms and out of suspicion.","category":"social"},{"name":"Ledger Forgery","description":"Reproduces wind-debt entries in a convincing hand.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_alder","name":"Wren Alder","description":"A young, freckled miller's daughter from the Hollow who works as the manor's under-cook for the weekend. She wears flour-dusted aprons and keeps a notebook of recipes and overheard gossip.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect her family's mill from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Find proof of the levy's unfairness that she can carry back to the Hollow Circle.","flaw":"Her curiosity makes her eavesdrop and meddle in matters beyond her station.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between loyalty to her family's secrecy and her wish to speak up for what she saw.","external_conflict":"Cassian Thorne holds her family's wind-debt and threatens to call it in if she talks.","arc":"Starts timid and hiding what she overheard in the pantry. When Cassian threatens her family's mill, she chooses to hand her notebook to Odalys. She ends emboldened, testifying openly and winning the Circle's respect.","personality_traits":["curious","kind","nervous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Unseen Servant","description":"Moves through the manor unnoticed and hears what others miss.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_hollis","name":"Bram Hollis","description":"A broad, soot-marked cable-braider from Emberroost who serves as the manor's caretaker for the season. Gruff and loyal, he has maintained the manor's skybridge anchor for twenty years.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the bridge anchor safe and the manor's skybridge from being blamed for the crime.","goal":"Prove the severed bridge cable was cut deliberately and not through Warden negligence.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders leads him to withhold information from anyone but his own.","internal_conflict":"He hides that he left the shielded forge-pit unattended the night of the murder, and feels guilty about it.","external_conflict":"Cartel guests accuse him of neglect, and the open-flame rule makes the unattended pit look damning.","arc":"Starts defensive and silent about his lapse. When Odalys, his old inspector, shows the cable cut was deliberate, he confesses where he was that night. He ends trusted by the guests and restored in his own eyes.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs skybridge cable with expert speed.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_odalys_cassian","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_venn","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Odalys Venn distrusts Cassian Thorne as a Cartel broker whose toll schemes harm the Wardens, and her suspicion of him drives the investigation."},{"id":"rel_cassian_wren","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","target_character_id":"chr_wren_alder","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Cassian Thorne holds Wren Alder's family wind-debt and threatens to call it in, pressuring her to stay silent about what she overheard."},{"id":"rel_wren_odalys","source_character_id":"chr_wren_alder","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_venn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Alder eventually trusts Odalys Venn with her notebook of overheard gossip, giving the investigation its key evidence."},{"id":"rel_bram_odalys","source_character_id":"chr_bram_hollis","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_venn","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Bram Hollis served under Odalys Venn's inspections for years and respects her, though his guilt keeps him from confiding in her at first."},{"id":"rel_cassian_bram","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","target_character_id":"chr_bram_hollis","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Cassian Thorne frames Bram Hollis for the severed cable, using the unattended forge-pit to deflect blame from himself."}]}
