es order over compassion and treats every unknown as a threat.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the signals are real and fears that admitting it would undermine the control she has built.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy dispute with the Drift Cartel strains her resources, and Mara's cabin becomes a convenient target for blame.","arc":"Edda begins as a rigid enforcer who treats the broadcasts as defiance. When she overhears her own name in a future transmission during a levy inspection, she is forced to confront her fear of the unexplained. She ends by lowering the ledger and standing guard at the cabin, trading control for protection.","personality_traits":["rigid","suspicious","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Authority","description":"Her accounting power can freeze a household's access to grain and supplies.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobias_bond","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Voss trusts Tobias Wren as her only visitor, but her future voice names him as a victim, so their friendship becomes a source of dread and guilt."},{"id":"rel_edda_mara_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edda Marsh pressures Mara Voss with levy demands and threats to confiscate her transmitter, amplifying Mara's isolation and fear."},{"id":"rel_edda_tobias_spy","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Edda Marsh, as Tobias Wren's overseer, forces him to spy on Mara, pitting his loyalty to the guild against his friendship with her."}]}
