on":"A young miller's apprentice in his early twenties who delivers ground grain to Mara's cabin each week. Lanky, freckled, with flour-dusted sleeves and a nervous habit of tugging his cap. He is the only person who regularly visits her.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"He wants to earn enough to repay his family's mounting wind-debt before the season ends.","goal":"Secure a permanent miller's licence by delivering grain on schedule to every remote home.","flaw":"He cannot say no to anyone and takes on risks he cannot handle.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between loyalty to his guild's levy demands and genuine care for Mara.","external_conflict":"His overseer expects him to report on Mara's grain use, and the night trips to the cabin are growing more dangerous.","arc":"Tobias starts as an eager pleaser who agrees to every errand. When the transmissions name him in Mara's voice and his overseer demands he report on her, he refuses the overseer for the first time and stays at the cabin overnight. He ends as someone who sets boundaries and chooses his own judgment over obedience.","personality_traits":["earnest","anxious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Knows the Hollow's windmills and grain routes intimately.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_edda_marsh","name":"Edda Marsh","description":"A stern overseer of the Hollow Circle in her fifties, responsible for collecting levies and tracking grain. She is broad-shouldered, grey-haired, and carries a ledger bound in cloudstone cord. She resents Mara's secrecy and the strange noises from her cabin.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"She wants to protect the Hollow Circle from Cartel pressure by keeping every household accountable.","goal":"Shut down Mara's broadcasts and seize the cabin's transmitter as collateral for unpaid wind-debt.","flaw":"She values order over compassion and treats every unknown as a threat.","internal_conflict":"She suspects the signals are real and fears that admitting it would undermine the control she has built.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy dispute with the Drift Cartel strains her resources, and Mara's cabin becomes a convenient target for blame.","arc":"Edda begins as a rigid enforcer who treats the broadcasts as defiance. When she overhears her own name in a future transmission during a levy inspection, she is forced to confront her fear of the unexplained. She ends by lowering the ledger and standing guard at the cabin, trading control for protection.","personality_traits":["rigid","suspicious","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Authority","description":"Her accounting power can freeze a household's access to grain and supplies.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobias_bond","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Voss trusts Tobias Wren as her only visitor, but her future voice names him as a victim, so their friendship becomes a source of dread and guilt."},{"id":"rel_edda_mara_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Edda Marsh pressures Mara Voss with levy demands and threats to confiscate her transmitter, amplifying Mara's isolation and fear."},{"id":"rel_edda_tobias_spy","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Edda Marsh, as Tobias Wren's overseer, forces him to spy on Mara, pitting his loyalty to the guild against his friendship with her."}]}
