{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A wiry woman in her late thirties with wind-chapped cheeks, a braided rope of salt-grey hair, and a scar across her left palm from a cut skybridge cable. Once the quartermaster of a Drift Cartel smuggling skiff, she turned herself in, served years of wind-debt labour, and now runs a modest cargo skiff out of Mistral Docks, wearing a faded captain's coat she refuses to mend.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To prove to herself and the isles that her past crimes are paid for, by returning the stolen map she once helped smuggle.","goal":"Recover the stolen skybridge map from the thief and deliver it to Silverspine Academy before the season's wind-debt deadline.","flaw":"She assumes she must carry every burden alone and hides the truth of her plans from allies.","internal_conflict":"She wants atonement but secretly misses the thrill of piracy and fears she is still the person she was.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants her back in service and will seize her skiff if she fails to repay her wind-debt.","arc":"Begins as a secretive loner repaying debts in silence. At Emberroost, when Brannoch Ashgrove offers to help and she is forced to trust him to cross a failing skybridge, she shares the whole plan. She ends the story as a captain who leads a crew openly and accepts help without seeing it as weakness.","personality_traits":["wry","guarded","resourceful","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind Reading","description":"Senses shifts in wind currents and predicts storms and drift paths.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Smuggler's Network","description":"Knows dock informants and back-channel routes across the isles.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_drake","name":"Orsolya Drake","role":"antagonist","description":"A silver-haired merchant princess in her fifties of the Drift Cartel, she dresses in tailored indigo coats and wears rings made of cut cloudstone. She rose through the Cartel Charter's loopholes and now governs shipping lanes from a glass-walled office above Mistral Docks.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure total Cartel control over every skybridge route so no rival can ever undercut her family's fortune.","goal":"Obtain the stolen map to learn undocumented skybridge routes and impose new tolls on them.","flaw":"She is incapable of seeing people as anything but assets and debts.","internal_conflict":"She fears the Cartel she built will collapse without her and cannot delegate or trust successors.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and the Grain Levy have turned the Wardens and the Hollow Circle against her, threatening her monopoly.","arc":"Starts as a confident monopolist certain that coercion is enough. When Hollow Circle farmers refuse the grain levy and her own captains begin defecting after Kestrel's open challenge, she has to bargain rather than command. She ends reduced in power but forced to accept a negotiated toll cap.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","ruthless","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Uses wind-debt records to coerce people into service.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_brannoch_ashgrove","name":"Brannoch Ashgrove","role":"supporting","description":"A broad, soot-stained Bridge Warden engineer in his forties with burn-scarred forearms and a gentle voice. He braids cloudstone cable at Emberroost and keeps a notebook of every bridge he has repaired.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and free of crushing tolls so ordinary travellers can cross.","goal":"Find the stolen map so the Wardens can repair neglected bridges before they fail.","flaw":"He rigidly follows Warden protocol and refuses any plan that bends a rule.","internal_conflict":"He values the fire-ban rules but knows they leave some failing bridges unrepaired.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls are starving Warden budgets, and his superiors forbid cooperation with ex-pirates.","arc":"Begins as a by-the-book engineer who distrusts Kestrel. When a bridge starts to fail and only her improvised, rule-bending rigging saves the crossing, he sets aside protocol. He ends by openly vouching for her before the Wardens.","personality_traits":["methodical","kind","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone cable under pressure.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_lyssa_thorne","name":"Lyssa Thorne","role":"supporting","description":"A sharp-eyed cartographer in her twenties at Silverspine Academy, with ink-stained fingers and a satchel of half-finished charts. She is the one who originally drew the stolen map.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To recover her life's work and clear her name after being blamed for its theft.","goal":"Join Kestrel's voyage and identify the map's forgery marks to prove it was stolen.","flaw":"She is reckless with her own safety when chasing answers.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between academic caution and the adventurous life she envies in Kestrel.","external_conflict":"The Academy council suspects her of selling the map to the Cartel.","arc":"Starts as a sheltered scholar hiding in her archives. When the Cartel's agents ambush her at Silverspine, she chooses to leave with Kestrel's crew. She ends by testifying publicly and becoming a field cartographer who balances boldness with caution.","personality_traits":["curious","brilliant","impulsive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Reads and charts shifting skybridge networks.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_marrow","name":"Pell Marrow","role":"supporting","description":"A lean, weathered miller from The Hollow in his sixties with flour-dusted sleeves and a quiet laugh. He once sold grain to Kestrel's old crew and knows the island's wind routes.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect The Hollow's farmers from the Cartel's grain levy.","goal":"Trade shelter and information to Kestrel in exchange for her help moving grain around Cartel tolls.","flaw":"He clings to old grudges and withholds help from anyone tied to piracy.","internal_conflict":"He resents Kestrel's past but needs her skills to save his community.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens to ruin the Hollow's harvest.","arc":"Starts bitter toward ex-pirates. When Kestrel risks her skiff to smuggle his grain past a Cartel blockade, he forgives her. He ends by guiding her crew to the hidden route that leads to the thief.","personality_traits":["dry","loyal","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Knows local wind patterns and hidden approaches around The Hollow.","category":"other"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kestrel_orsolya","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_drake","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Drake holds Kestrel Vane's wind-debt and wants her back in Cartel service, using it to force her to surrender the map."},{"id":"rel_kestrel_brannoch","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_brannoch_ashgrove","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Kestrel Vane and Brannoch Ashgrove begin as wary rivals over bridge safety rules, but grow into allies as she earns his trust."},{"id":"rel_lyssa_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_lyssa_thorne","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Lyssa Thorne seeks Kestrel Vane's protection and ship to recover her map, while Kestrel needs Lyssa's cartography skill to authenticate it."},{"id":"rel_pell_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_pell_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Pell Marrow distrusts Kestrel Vane for her piracy past, creating friction until she proves herself by running his grain past the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_pell","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_drake","target_character_id":"chr_pell_marrow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Drake imposes the grain levy on Pell Marrow's Hollow Circle, driving him to side with Kestrel Vane."}]}
