{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_marisol_vane","name":"Marisol Vane","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered caravan-mistress in her late forties who has led her skyward merchant caravan across the skybridges for twenty years. Born on The Hollow to a milling family, she carries flour-dusted scarves in memory of home, has silver-streaked braids, rope-scarred hands, and a warm, gravelly laugh that settles anxious crews.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the caravan crew, who are her found family, fed, paid, and safe through the season.","goal":"Deliver the caravan's grain and goods across the contested bridges and clear the crew's mounting wind-debt before the season ends.","flaw":"She shoulders every burden alone and refuses help, mistaking self-sacrifice for leadership.","internal_conflict":"She longs to retire to quiet life on The Hollow but fears the crew cannot survive without her.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's Grain Levy and bridge tolls threaten to bankrupt her caravan while both sides of the Toll War court or coerce her.","arc":"Starts as a lone, overworked leader who hides the caravan's debts from her crew. When a Cartel levy forces her to either abandon a stranded bridge-crossing or confess the debt, she tells the crew everything and lets them vote on the route. She ends as a leader who shares command and trusts her successor.","personality_traits":["warm","stubborn","protective","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind-reading","description":"Predicts gusts and drift patterns from the sway of cables and the feel of the air.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Hard bargaining","description":"Negotiates tolls and wind-debt terms with suspicious officials.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_reck","name":"Tobin Reck","role":"supporting","description":"A lanky, freckled young rigger of nineteen with soot-stained sleeves, apprenticed to Marisol after fleeing a Cartel dockyard. He wears a battered brass whistle and talks quickly when nervous.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To prove he is more than the debt-bonded dockhand the Cartel made him.","goal":"Earn his full caravan share and buy out his family's Cartel indenture.","flaw":"He is impulsive and leaps to action before thinking through consequences.","internal_conflict":"He is grateful to Marisol yet tempted by the Cartel's offer to free his family if he informs on her.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents at Mistral Docks hold his family's indenture and demand he report the caravan's routes.","arc":"Starts as an eager, reckless rigger secretly feeding route details to Cartel agents. When a frayed cable on a bridge nearly drops the caravan, he realizes his reports endanger the crew. He confesses to Marisol and feeds the Cartel false routes, ending as a trusted, deliberate rigger.","personality_traits":["eager","anxious","loyal","quick-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable rigging","description":"Quickly secures and repairs skybridge cables and cargo harnesses.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ilvane_dross","name":"Ilvane Dross","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished Cartel factor in her fifties with rings of cloudstone on each finger, immaculate grey robes, and a courteous smile that never reaches her eyes. She rose from a Mistral Docks clerk to oversee shipping lanes and levies.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's total dominion over inter-isle trade so she can never be poor again.","goal":"Seize the caravan's grain cargo and force Marisol into Cartel service through the levy.","flaw":"She is controlling and cannot tolerate any trade she does not oversee.","internal_conflict":"She privately doubts the Cartel's greed will survive another Toll War but cannot admit it without losing her standing.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle and the Bridge Wardens resist her levies, and Marisol's caravan stands in her way.","arc":"Starts as a confident enforcer certain that control equals safety. When Wardens close a bridge during the Toll War and strand her own cargo, she must accept the caravan's aid. She ends by grudgingly negotiating a fair levy, loosening her grip.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","patient","proud"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger mastery","description":"Tracks debts, tolls, and levies across the whole archipelago in her head.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cartel leverage","description":"Calls on Cartel enforcers and harbour officials to pressure rivals.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_halvard","name":"Oren Halvard","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer in his sixties with a grey beard braided with cloudstone thread and a limp from an old cable snap. He speaks slowly and keeps a notebook of every bridge's tension.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge intact so no more lives are lost to failing cables.","goal":"Hold the Wardens' toll line while guiding the caravan safely across the weakest bridges.","flaw":"He is rigid and distrusts anyone who profits from the bridges he guards.","internal_conflict":"His duty to enforce tolls conflicts with his sympathy for struggling merchants like Marisol.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's rising tolls make merchants resent the Wardens, and his superiors order him to turn the caravan back.","arc":"Starts as a by-the-book Warden who sees merchants as threats. When Marisol's crew helps him repair a sparking bridge anchor, he defies orders to let the caravan cross and ends as a bridge-keeper who bends rules for people.","personality_traits":["stern","meticulous","honorable"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tension sense","description":"Judges a skybridge's strain by touch and sound.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Forge-pit craf