el dockyard. He wears a battered brass whistle and talks quickly when nervous.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To prove he is more than the debt-bonded dockhand the Cartel made him.","goal":"Earn his full caravan share and buy out his family's Cartel indenture.","flaw":"He is impulsive and leaps to action before thinking through consequences.","internal_conflict":"He is grateful to Marisol yet tempted by the Cartel's offer to free his family if he informs on her.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents at Mistral Docks hold his family's indenture and demand he report the caravan's routes.","arc":"Starts as an eager, reckless rigger secretly feeding route details to Cartel agents. When a frayed cable on a bridge nearly drops the caravan, he realizes his reports endanger the crew. He confesses to Marisol and feeds the Cartel false routes, ending as a trusted, deliberate rigger.","personality_traits":["eager","anxious","loyal","quick-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable rigging","description":"Quickly secures and repairs skybridge cables and cargo harnesses.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ilvane_dross","name":"Ilvane Dross","role":"antagonist","description":"A polished Cartel factor in her fifties with rings of cloudstone on each finger, immaculate grey robes, and a courteous smile that never reaches her eyes. She rose from a Mistral Docks clerk to oversee shipping lanes and levies.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's total dominion over inter-isle trade so she can never be poor again.","goal":"Seize the caravan's grain cargo and force Marisol into Cartel service through the levy.","flaw":"She is controlling and cannot tolerate any trade she does not oversee.","internal_conflict":"She privately doubts the Cartel's greed will survive another Toll War but cannot admit it without losing her standing.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle and t